<https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Core/ExternalIdentifierType/ibrn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "International Business Registration Number (IBRN) <https://ekys.org/business_identifiers/> is a unique identifier for legal entities standardized by ISO 8000-116 <https://www.iso.org/standard/75117.html>. It is composed of two parts: a jurisdiction prefix and a local authoritative legal entity identifier (ALEI), separated by a colon. The prefix contains an ISO 3166 country code, an optional subdivision code, and a register code (e.g., US-DE.BER:3031657)."@en .
_:N02b59c0986d24c34af8029a215ac99e5 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> _:N7fc1a5957c0c4a5da1187997e2a56762 .
