<https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Security/ExploitCatalogVulnAssessmentRelationship> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "An ExploitCatalogVulnAssessmentRelationship describes if a vulnerability is\nlisted in any exploit catalog such as the\nCISA Known Exploited Vulnerabilities (KEV) Catalog <https://www.cisa.gov/known-exploited-vulnerabilities-catalog>.\n\n*Constraints*\n\n- The relationship type shall be set to hasAssessmentFor.\n\n*Example*\n\n{\n  \"type\": \"security_ExploitCatalogVulnAssessmentRelationship\",\n  \"spdxId\": \"urn:spdx.dev:exploit-catalog-1\",\n  \"relationshipType\": \"hasAssessmentFor\",\n  \"security_catalogType\": \"kev\",\n  \"locator\": \"https://www.cisa.gov/known-exploited-vulnerabilities-catalog\",\n  \"security_exploited\": \"true\",\n  \"from\": \"urn:spdx.dev:vuln-cve-2023-2136\",\n  \"to\": [\"urn:product-google-chrome-112.0.5615.136\"],\n  \"suppliedBy\": \"urn:spdx.dev:agent-jane-doe\",\n  \"security_publishedTime\": \"2021-03-09T11:04:53Z\"\n}"@en .
<https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Core/ExternalIdentifierType/ibid> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "International Business Identifier (IBID) <https://ekys.org/business_identifiers/> is a verifiable unique identifier for legal entities as defined in the ISO/DIS 25500-3 <https://www.iso.org/standard/87705.html> draft standard. It is composed of three data elements: the International Business Registration Number (IBRN), the legal name, and the date of origin formatted as eight numeric characters (YYYYMMDD). Each element is separated by a pipe character (|) (e.g., US-DE.BER:3031657|Code Management Association|19990420)."@en .
